message.content:
I can see the vulnerability. In `getFirstTLVRecord`, the code does:
```cpp
TLVRecordType resRec(tlvDataBasePtr); // for NRVO optimization
// resRec pointer is out-bounds of the TLV records memory
if (resRec.getRecordBasePtr() + resRec.getTotalSize() > tlvDataBasePtr + tlvDataLen)
    resRec.assign(NULL);
```

The `TLVRecordType` constructor reads `recordType` and `recordLen` from the data. If `tlvDataLen` is less than the size of `TLVRawData` (which is `recordType` + `recordLen`), then reading `recordType` and `recordLen` will cause a heap-buffer-overflow READ.

Let me look at the `TLVRecord` constructor and `getTotalSize`:

